{{also|fljuga}}
==Icelandic==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|non|is}} {{term|fljúga|lang=non}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|is}} {{recons|fleuganan|lang=gem-pro}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|is}} {{recons|pleuk-|lang=ine-pro}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈfljuːa/|lang=is}}
*: {{rhymes|uːa|lang=is}}

===Verb===
{{is-verb-strong|flaug|flugu|flogið}}

# {{intransitive|lang=is}} to [[fly]]

====Conjugation====
{{is-conj-s2|fl|jú|g}}

====Derived terms====
* {{l|is|fljúga út}} (to [[sell like hotcakes]])
* {{l|is|fljúgandi}} (flying)
* {{l|is|fljúgandi hálka}} (slippery ice)
* {{l|is|fljúgast}}
* {{l|is|fljúgast á}} (to wrestle, to scuffle)
* {{l|is|floginn}} (vanished)
* {{l|is|sveltur sitjandi kráka en fljúgandi fær}}
* {{l|is|tíminn flýgur}}

