==Old Norse==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|gem-pro|non}} {{recons|fleuganan|lang=gem-pro}}. Cognate with Old English ''[[fleogan|flēoġan]]'' (Modern English ''[[fly]]''), Old Frisian ''[[fliaga|fliāga]]'' (Saterland Frisian {{term|fljooge|lang=stq}}), Old Saxon {{term|fliogan|lang=osx}} (Low German {{term|flegen|lang=nds}}), Old Dutch {{term|fliogan|lang=odt}} (Dutch [[vliegen]]), Old High German {{term|fliogan|lang=goh}} (German ''[[fliegen]]''). Ultimately from {{etyl|ine-pro|non}} {{recons|pleuk-|lang=ine-pro}}. Indo-European cognates include Lithuanian ''[[plaũkti]]''.

===Verb===
{{head|non|verb}}

# to [[fly]]

